# The read must FAIL: Surelog reports UH0734 on the three ILLEGAL selects in
# dut.sv -- a variable index in a continuous-assignment target, and the two
# bounds `n` of part-selects whose other bound is the constant 0 (the width
# varies with n).  The exact count pins it to those lines: the genvar-indexed
# targets, the parameter-bounded slice and `acc[i+1 -: 2]` must stay silent.
logger -expect error "Surelog reported 0 fatal, 0 syntax and 3 other error" 1
read_sv -nonote -noinfo -nowarning dut.sv
